Title: THE LAST LIGHT
Credit: Written by
Author: Coil

INT. PROJECTION ROOM - NIGHT

A reel turns slowly. MAYA holds a strip of film up to the light.

MAYA
Every frame remembers something we forgot.

ELI
Then let it run. We have until morning.

Maya threads the film through the projector. Dust catches the beam.

EXT. CINEMA - DAWN

The marquee goes dark as the first commuters cross the street.

MAYA
There's always another showing.
